#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:3
msgid "格子定数をどう求めるか：Cuのエネルギー曲線と応力"
msgstr "Determining the Lattice Constant of Cu from Energy and Stress"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:5
msgid ""
"結晶の格子定数は、全エネルギーが最小になる格子の大きさとして求めます。\\ よく使われる求め方は2つあります。\\ "
"1つは、格子定数を少しずつ変えて全エネルギーを計算し、その曲線の極小を探す方法です。\\ "
"もう1つは、1回の計算で求まる応力（圧力）を手がかりに、圧力が0になるまで格子を自動で動かす方法（QEの ``vc-relax`` "
"、Quloudの計算機能「格子定数最適化」）です。"
msgstr ""
"The lattice constant of a crystal is the lattice size at which its total "
"energy is lowest. \\ Two methods are commonly used to find it. \\ One is "
"to calculate the total energy at a series of closely spaced lattice "
"constants and find the minimum of the resulting curve. \\ The other uses "
"the stress (pressure) obtained from a single calculation to guide "
"automatic changes to the lattice until the pressure reaches zero. This is"
" QE's ``vc-relax``, called \"Lattice Optimization\" in Quloud."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:10
msgid ""
"どちらも同じ極小を目指しているはずですが、曲線の当てはめ方や計算の条件によって、得られる値は少しずつ違います。\\ "
"本稿では、面心立方（fcc）構造の銅（Cu）について、2つの求め方で格子定数を0.001 Åの桁まで求め、値がどれだけ、なぜ違うのかを調べます。"
msgstr ""
"Both methods should locate the same minimum, but the values they give "
"differ slightly depending on how the curve is fitted and on the "
"calculation conditions. \\ Here we use both methods to determine the "
"lattice constant of face-centered cubic (fcc) copper (Cu) to the nearest "
"0.001 Å and examine how much the values differ and why."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:14
msgid "計算対象と計算条件"
msgstr "Systems and Calculation Conditions"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:16
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"計算するのは、fccのCuの原始胞（1原子）です。\\ 原始胞は、3辺の長さが立方晶の格子定数 :math:`a` の "
":math:`1/\\sqrt{2}` で、辺のなす角がすべて60°のセルです（慣用胞と原始胞の関係は、技術ノートの\\ `格子基底と座標系の変換"
" <https://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/lattice_transform.html>`__\\ "
"を参照してください）。\\ 以下では、格子の大きさを立方晶の格子定数 :math:`a` "
"で表し、エネルギーは1原子あたりの値、圧力はQEの出力どおりkbar（10 kbar = 1 GPa）で示します。\\ 計算条件を :numref"
":`tab-cl-conditions` にまとめます。"
msgstr ""
"We use the one-atom primitive cell of fcc Cu. \\ All three edges have "
"length equal to the cubic lattice constant :math:`a` multiplied by "
":math:`1/\\sqrt{2}`, and all angles between the edges are 60°. For how "
"the conventional cell relates to the primitive cell, see \\ `Lattice "
"Basis and Coordinate System Transformations <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/lattice_transform.html>`__ \\ in the Technical "
"Notes. \\ We describe the lattice size using the cubic lattice constant "
":math:`a`, report energies per atom, and give pressures in kbar as in the"
" QE output (10 kbar = 1 GPa). \\ The calculation conditions are listed in"
" :numref:`tab-cl-conditions`."

