#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:105
msgid ""
"左：2次式（破線は4点、実線は12点で当てはめたもの）と、SCFのエネルギー（青い点）の、Birch–Murnaghanの式の曲線からの差。右：2次式で求めた"
" :math:`a_0` と当てはめた点の数。破線はBirch–Murnaghanの式（13点）の :math:`a_0` です。"
msgstr ""
"Left: differences from the Birch–Murnaghan curve for the quadratic fits "
"(dashed for 4 points, solid for 12 points) and the SCF energies "
"(blue points). Right: :math:`a_0` from each quadratic fit versus the "
"number of points fitted. The dashed line marks :math:`a_0` from the "
"Birch–Murnaghan fit to 13 points."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:107
msgid ""
"範囲を広げるほど、 :math:`a_0` は大きい側へずれていき、12点では4点より0.004 Å大きくなります。\\ "
"左の図のように、2次式は左右対称な放物線なので、縮めた側の急な立ち上がりと伸ばした側のゆるやかな立ち上がりの両方に合わせようとして、頂点が伸ばした側へずれます。\\"
" 範囲を狭めればずれは小さくなりますが、点が少なく、エネルギー差も小さくなるので、1点ごとの数値誤差の影響を受けやすくなります。\\ "
"2次式で求めた値は、どの範囲で当てはめたかを添えないと意味がありません。"
msgstr ""
"As the range widens, :math:`a_0` shifts to larger values. The fit to 12 "
"points gave a value 0.004 Å higher than the fit to 4 points. \\ As the "
"left panel shows, the quadratic is a symmetric parabola. Fitting both the"
" steep rise on the compressed side and the gentler rise on the expanded "
"side shifts its vertex toward the expanded side. \\ Narrowing the range "
"reduces the shift, but with fewer points and smaller energy differences, "
"numerical errors at individual points have more influence. \\ A value "
"from a quadratic fit is meaningless without the fitting range."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:115
msgid "状態方程式"
msgstr "Equation of State"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:117
msgid ""
"非対称な曲線を表すために、固体の圧縮についての状態方程式を使います。\\ ここでは、体積 :math:`V` （1原子あたり、fccでは "
":math:`V=a^3/4` ）の関数として、よく使われる2つの式を当てはめます。\\ :math:`E_0` は極小のエネルギー、 "
":math:`V_0` は極小の体積、 :math:`B_0` は体積弾性率、 :math:`B_0'` はその圧力微分です。"
msgstr ""
"We use an equation of state for solid compression to describe the "
"asymmetric curve. \\ We fit two commonly used forms as functions of the "
"volume :math:`V` per atom, where :math:`V=a^3/4` for fcc. \\ :math:`E_0` "
"is the minimum energy, :math:`V_0` is the volume at the minimum, "
":math:`B_0` is the bulk modulus, and :math:`B_0'` is its pressure "
"derivative."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:121
msgid "Murnaghanの式 [6]_ は、体積弾性率が圧力に比例して増える（ :math:`B=B_0+B_0'P` ）と仮定したものです。"
msgstr ""
"The Murnaghan equation [6]_ assumes that the bulk modulus increases "
"linearly with pressure (:math:`B=B_0+B_0'P`)."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:123
msgid "E(V)=E_0+\\frac{B_0V}{B_0'}\\left[\\frac{(V_0/V)^{B_0'}}{B_0'-1}+1\\right]-\\frac{B_0V_0}{B_0'-1}"
msgstr "E(V)=E_0+\\frac{B_0V}{B_0'}\\left[\\frac{(V_0/V)^{B_0'}}{B_0'-1}+1\\right]-\\frac{B_0V_0}{B_0'-1}"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:128
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"3次のBirch–Murnaghanの式 [7]_ は、有限ひずみ "
":math:`f=\\frac12\\left[(V_0/V)^{2/3}-1\\right]` の3次までの展開です。"
msgstr ""
"The third-order Birch–Murnaghan equation [7]_ is an expansion to third "
"order in the finite strain "
":math:`f=\\frac12\\left[(V_0/V)^{2/3}-1\\right]`."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:130
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"E(V)=E_0+\\frac{9V_0B_0}{16}\\left\\{\\left[\\left(\\frac{V_0}{V}\\right)^{2/3}-1\\right]^3B_0'"
"\n"
"+\\left[\\left(\\frac{V_0}{V}\\right)^{2/3}-1\\right]^2\\left[6-4\\left(\\frac{V_0}{V}\\right)^{2/3}\\right]\\right\\}"
msgstr ""
"E(V)=E_0+\\frac{9V_0B_0}{16}\\left\\{\\left[\\left(\\frac{V_0}{V}\\right)^{2/3}-1\\right]^3B_0'"
"\n"
"+\\left[\\left(\\frac{V_0}{V}\\right)^{2/3}-1\\right]^2\\left[6-4\\left(\\frac{V_0}{V}\\right)^{2/3}\\right]\\right\\}"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:136
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"式 :eq:`cl-bm3` は :math:`x=V^{-2/3}` の3次多項式なので、通常の多項式の最小二乗で当てはめられます。\\ 式 "
":eq:`cl-murnaghan` は、 :math:`V_0` と :math:`B_0'` を決めると :math:`E_0` と "
":math:`B_0` について1次式になるので、 :math:`V_0` と :math:`B_0'` "
"だけを探索しました（解析スクリプトはNumPyだけで動きます。 :doc:`reproduction` ）。"
msgstr ""
"Equation :eq:`cl-bm3` is cubic in :math:`x=V^{-2/3}`, so it can be fitted"
" by ordinary polynomial least squares. \\ In Equation :eq:`cl-murnaghan`,"
" fixing :math:`V_0` and :math:`B_0'` makes it linear in :math:`E_0` and "
":math:`B_0`, so we searched only over :math:`V_0` and :math:`B_0'` (the "
"analysis script needs only NumPy; see :doc:`reproduction`)."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:139
msgid "状態方程式の当てはめで求めた格子定数 :math:`a_0` 、体積弾性率 :math:`B_0` 、その圧力微分 :math:`B_0'`"
msgstr ""
"Lattice constant :math:`a_0`, bulk modulus :math:`B_0`, and its pressure "
"derivative :math:`B_0'` from equation-of-state fits"

