#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:165
msgid ""
"表の7点は、13点のうち3.58〜3.70 Åの範囲の点です。\\ 2つの式の :math:`a_0` の差は0.0001 "
"Åで、Birch–Murnaghanの式では当てはめる範囲を13点から7点に狭めても :math:`a_0` は変わりません。\\ "
"Birch–Murnaghanの式のほうが残差が1桁小さく、13点のエネルギーを0.005 meV以内で再現します。\\ "
"2次式と違い、状態方程式は範囲を広げても値がずれないので、極小から離れた点も含めて安定に :math:`a_0` を決められます。\\ "
"以下では、Birch–Murnaghanの式の値 :math:`a_0=3.6303` Åを、エネルギー曲線から求めた格子定数とします。"
msgstr ""
"The 7-point fit in the table uses the points from 3.58 to 3.70 Å out of "
"the original 13. \\ Fitting the two equations gives values of :math:`a_0`"
" that differ by 0.0001 Å, and for Birch–Murnaghan, narrowing the fitting "
"range from 13 to 7 points leaves :math:`a_0` unchanged. \\ The "
"Birch–Murnaghan equation gives residuals an order of magnitude smaller "
"and reproduces the energies of all 13 points to within 0.005 meV. \\ "
"Unlike the quadratic fit, the equation of state gives a consistent "
":math:`a_0` as the fitting range widens, so we can include points farther"
" from the minimum and still obtain a stable value. \\ We use the "
"Birch–Murnaghan result :math:`a_0=3.6303` Å as the lattice constant "
"obtained from the energy curve."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:174
msgid "圧力とエネルギー曲線"
msgstr "Pressure and the Energy Curve"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:176
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"SCF計算の出力の圧力 :math:`P` （ ``P=`` ）は、波動関数から直接計算した応力で、エネルギーの体積微分 "
":math:`P=-\\mathrm{d}E/\\mathrm{d}V` にあたります。\\ :numref:`fig-cl-eos` "
"の右の図で、SCFの圧力（青い点）と、当てはめた曲線を微分した圧力（灰色の曲線）はよく重なっています。\\ "
"SCFの圧力から当てはめた曲線の圧力を引くと、13点すべてで −0.67〜−0.33 kbar、極小付近では −0.44 "
"kbarで、SCFの圧力がわずかに小さくなっています。\\ SCFの圧力が0になる格子定数は3.6298 Åで、エネルギー曲線の極小（3.6303"
" Å）より0.0005 Å小さくなります。\\ 極小付近では、圧力は格子定数1 Åあたり約1100 kbar変わるので、0.44 "
"kbarの差が格子定数の0.0004 Åに相当します。"
msgstr ""
"The pressure :math:`P` (``P=``) in the SCF output comes directly from the"
" stress calculated from the wave functions and corresponds to the volume "
"derivative of the energy, :math:`P=-\\mathrm{d}E/\\mathrm{d}V`. \\ "
":numref:`fig-cl-eos` (right) shows that the SCF pressures (blue points) "
"nearly overlap with the pressure obtained by differentiating the fit "
"(gray curve). \\ Subtracting the fitted pressure from the SCF pressure "
"gives differences from −0.67 to −0.33 kbar across all 13 points and −0.44"
" kbar near the minimum. The SCF pressure is slightly lower. \\ The SCF "
"pressure reaches zero at 3.6298 Å, which is 0.0005 Å below the energy "
"curve minimum (3.6303 Å). \\ Near the minimum, the pressure changes by "
"about 1100 kbar per 1 Å change in lattice constant, so a difference of "
"0.44 kbar corresponds to 0.0004 Å in the lattice constant."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:182
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"この差は、平面波の数が有限であることから生じます。\\ "
"エネルギー曲線は、カットオフエネルギーを一定にして計算しているので、格子を変えると平面波の数が変わります。\\ "
"一方、SCFの応力は、平面波の組を固定したまま格子をわずかに変えたときのエネルギー変化として計算されます。\\ "
"平面波が十分に多ければ両者は一致しますが、そうでなければ差が残ります。この差を **Pulay応力** （有限基底による応力の補正）と呼びます "
"[8]_ 。\\ :numref:`{number}節 <sec-cl-cutoff>` "
"で、この差がカットオフエネルギーとともにどう変わるかを調べます。"
msgstr ""
"The difference arises from the finite number of plane waves. \\ We "
"compute the energy curve at a fixed cutoff energy, so changing the "
"lattice changes the number of plane waves. \\ The SCF stress, however, "
"comes from the energy change for a small change in the lattice while "
"holding the set of plane waves fixed. \\ The two results agree when there"
" are enough plane waves, but otherwise a difference remains. This "
"difference is called **Pulay stress**, a correction to the stress due to "
"the finite basis [8]_. \\ :numref:`Section {number} <sec-cl-cutoff>` "
"examines how this difference varies with the cutoff energy."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:191
msgid "vc-relax（格子定数最適化）"
msgstr "vc-relax (Lattice Constant Optimization)"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:193
msgid ""
"QEの ``vc-relax`` は、SCF計算で求めた応力を使い、BFGS法で圧力が0になる格子を探します。\\ "
"Quloudでは、計算機能「格子定数最適化」がこの計算です。\\ 応力の収束閾値は0.01 GPa（0.1 kbar）にしました。\\ "
"3.56、3.64、3.72 Åの3つから始めたときの格子定数の変化を :numref:`fig-cl-cutoff` の右に、結果を "
":numref:`tab-cl-vcrelax` に示します。"
msgstr ""
"QE's ``vc-relax`` uses the stress from SCF calculations and the BFGS "
"method to find the lattice at zero pressure. \\ In Quloud, this is the "
"\"Lattice Optimization\" feature. \\ We set the stress convergence "
"threshold to 0.01 GPa (0.1 kbar). \\ The right panel of :numref:`fig-cl-"
"cutoff` shows how the lattice constant changes from the three starting "
"values 3.56, 3.64, and 3.72 Å. The final results are in :numref:`tab-cl-"
"vcrelax`."

